aving","pg_ayala"],"evidence_status":"attributed_research_summary","sort_order":1},{"id":"puerto_galera_discovery_8","place_i_d":"oriental_mindoro_puerto_galera","suggested_mission":8,"title":"Events and their historical meaning","category":"historical_events","text":"Puerto Galera was nominated as a UNESCO biosphere reserve in 1977, a milestone in the history of its relationship with the surrounding landscape. Read this as the specific event or remembered account described, not an automatic first-settlement or discovery date.","question":"What does this historical record allow us to conclude?","answer":"Only the specific event or account it describes","options":["Only the specific event or account it describes","That nobody lived there before it","That every tradition began on that date","That one outsider discovered the place"],"source_i_ds":["pg_unesco"],"evidence_status":"web_documented","sort_order":2},{"id":"puerto_galera_discovery_9","place_i_d":"oriental_mindoro_puerto_galera","suggested_mission":9,"title":"Community memory across generations","category":"community_memory","text":"Iraya-Mangyan artisans pass nito-weaving skills through families, making baskets, trays and other useful objects. This tradition belongs to its community of makers. Preserve the source’s distinction between a remembered story and a documented practice. Do not assign one community’s knowledge to all residents.","question":"How should this local memory or practice be described?","answer":"With its attribution and limits, without claiming it represents every resident","options":["With its attribution and limits, without claiming it represents every resident","As a practice shared identically by every resident","As proof of a single founder for the whole municipality","Without naming the community or source"],"source_i_ds":["pg_weaving"],"evidence_status":"web_documented","sort_order":3},{"id":"puerto_galera_discovery_10","place_i_d":"oriental_mindoro_puerto_galera","suggested_mission"