account it describes","options":["Only the specific event or account it describes","That nobody lived there before it","That every tradition began on that date","That one outsider discovered the place"],"source_i_ds":["act3498"],"evidence_status":"web_documented","sort_order":72},{"id":"bulalacao_discovery_9","place_i_d":"oriental_mindoro_bulalacao","suggested_mission":9,"title":"Community memory across generations","category":"community_memory","text":"The town history preserves a bird story about Bulalacao's name and explicitly identifies it as a myth. Stories can carry identity without being treated as confirmed events. Preserve the source’s distinction between a remembered story and a documented practice. Do not assign one community’s knowledge to all residents.","question":"How should this local memory or practice be described?","answer":"With its attribution and limits, without claiming it represents every resident","options":["With its attribution and limits, without claiming it represents every resident","As a practice shared identically by every resident","As proof of a single founder for the whole municipality","Without naming the community or source"],"source_i_ds":["bulalacao_history"],"evidence_status":"oral_account","sort_order":73},{"id":"bulalacao_discovery_10","place_i_d":"oriental_mindoro_bulalacao","suggested_mission":10,"title":"History in its regional context","category":"regional_history","text":"Bulalacao belongs to a regional history with different kinds of milestones. The cited Act 3498 reestablishments took effect in 1929; Victoria’s formation is recorded in 1953; Socorro’s legal creation in 1963; and Calapan’s cityhood plebiscite in 1998. These events do not date the first habitation of each place. The dates are inherited citations awaiting fresh source verification.","question":"Which event is latest among these cited regional milestones?","answer":"Calapan’s cityhood plebiscite in 1998","options":["Calapan’s cityhood plebiscite in 1998","The Act 3498 reestablishments in 1929","Victoria’s formation in 1953","Socorro’s creation in 1963"],"source_i_ds":["act3498","victoria_history","socorro_law","calapan_history"],"evidence_status":"attributed_research_summary","sort_order":74},{"id":"puerto_galera_discovery_11","place_i_d":"oriental_mindoro_puerto_galera","suggested_mission":11,"title":"Living heritage and practical skills","category":"living_heritage","text":"Basket-making and the sharing of craft knowledge are documented in the cited Iraya-Mangyan community material. Specific patterns and demonstrations require maker consent.","question":"Which cultural theme or practical skill is named in this briefing?","answer":"Iraya-Mangyan nito weaving","options":["Iraya-Mangyan nito weaving","A tradition shared identically by every resident","A proven single discoverer of the municipality","Permission to reproduce every local design"],"source_i_ds":["pg_unesco","pg_weaving"],"evidence_status":"attributed_research_summary","sort_order":75},{"id":"puerto_galera_discovery_12","place_i_d":"oriental_mindoro_puerto_galera","suggested_mission":12,"title":"Identity and traveler values","category":"identity_and_values","text":"Puerto Galera: Basket-making and the sharing of craft knowledge are documented in the cited Iraya-Mangyan community material. Specific patterns and demonstrations require maker consent. In this adventure, practice these traveler values: Respect named-community attribution; Care for linked land and water habitats. These are learning goals, not a claim that all residents hold identical values.","question":"How should your traveler care for this heritage and identity?","answer":"Respect attribution, community differences, and appropriate permissions","options":["Respect attribution, community differences, and appropriate permissions","Treat every resident as following the same practice","Take real cultural objects as collectibles","Copy expressive material without checking permission"],"source_i_d